    "media:imagetext": "THE SATURDAY EVENING POST\nFamed for its Calypso\nSingers, beautiful scenery,\nand the great Pitch Lake which\nwas visited by Sir Walter\nRaleigh, TRINIDAD has\nover 170,000 Hindus.\nThis priest, born in India,\nhas lived in Trinidad\nfor 78 years. He, and\nother residents of this\nBritish Crown Colony,\nbuy many U.S. goods.\nFounded by the brother of Christopher Columbus in 1496, Ciudad\nTrujillo boasts a magnificent airport... And the DOMINICAN\nSoar now by CUPPER\nwhere Pirate ships once sailed!\nSir Francis Drake attacked\nPUERTO RICO in 1595 ...\nFrom here, Ponce de Leon sailed\nto discover Florida.\nThroughout the West Indies the tropical\nfruits are delicious! Besides those we know\nwell, like the banana and the lime, are\nmany others the mango, the papaya and\nthe chirimoya or custard apple.\nFar from the madding crowd, CUBA's Varadero Beach -five miles of it! -lies peacefully in trop-\nical sunshine. You reach it via Havana, Cuba's capital, only 90 minutes from Miami by Clipper.\nLargest of the British West Indies is JAMAICA, once governed by the ex-\npirate, Henry Morgan. At Montego Bay the sea is so crystal-clear you can see\na shilling on the bottom in fifteen feet of water.... Good food, excellent hotels.\nDo you know that you can now\nfly by Pan American direct\nfrom New York to San Juan, Puerto\nRico in only 8 hours, nonstop? :..\nthat you can fly from Miami to all\nthe major' islands of the Caribbean\nin just a few hours?\nFor information on Clipper travel\nnot only to the West Indies, but also\nto Latin America, Europe, Africa,\nAlaska, Hawaii or Australasia, see\nyour Travel Agent now-or the\nnearest Pan American office.\nPAN AMERICAN\nWORLD AIRWAYS\nPAA\nThe System of the Flying Clippers",
